                             **Auxiliary Sense:** TP10 (BBP), TP11 (BBN)\n    77\t\n    78\t**Temperature Sensing Components**\n                  
                             79\t*   **Pullup Resistors (10.0k):** R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19.\n    80\t*   **Thermistors               
                             (NTC):** RT1, RT2, RT3, RT4, RT5, RT6, RT7, RT8.\n    81\t*   **GPIO1 Filter:**\n    82\t    *                       
                             **R128:** 1.0k Resistor\n    83\t    *   **C60:** 1uF Capacitor\n    84\t    *   **D3:** 24V Dual                    
                             Zener/TVS Diode\n    85\t*   **DNP Components:** R20 (100k), C12 (DNP) on RT8 channel.\n    86\t\n                   
                             87\t# Connectivity & Signal Flow\n    88\t\n    89\t**Main IC (U1) Connections:**\n    90\t*   **Cell                
                             Inputs:** `VC0` through `VC16` connect to the cell voltage sense lines.\n    91\t*   **Balancing:**                  
                             `CB0` through `CB16` connect to the cell balance lines.\n    92\t*   **GPIOs:** `GPIO1` through `GPIO8`              
                             connect to the temperature sensing block (via J4).\n    93\t*   **Power Supply:**\n    94\t    *   `BAT`             
                             (Pin 1) is the high-voltage supply, filtered from the `PWR` net.\n    95\t    *   `AVDD`, `CVDD`, `DVDD`             
                             are internal regulator outputs tied together and decoupled to GND.\n    96\t    *   `TSREF` (Pin 51)                 
                             provides the reference voltage for the thermistors.\n    97\t    *   `LDOIN` (Pin 47), `NEG5V` (Pin 44),             
                             `NPNB` (Pin 48), `REFHP` (Pin 37) are additional regulator/reference pins.\n    98\t    *   **NPN Supply             
                             (Optional):** `LDOIN` is powered via an external NPN (Q1). `PWR` -> R4 -> R3 -> Q1(C). Q1(E) -> `LDOIN`.             
                             Base is driven by `NPNB`. C1 filters the Collector input.\n    99\t*   **Communication:**\n   100\t    *             
                             **Daisy Chain:** `COMHP`/`COMHN` (High side) and `COMLP`/`COMLN` (Low side) for stacking multiple BMS                
                             ICs.\n   101\t    *   **Local Host:** `RX` (Pin 52) and `TX` (Pin 53) for communication with a                       
                             microcontroller.\n   102\t    *   **Fault:** `NFAULT` (Pin 62) is an active-low fault output.\n   103\t*             
                             **Grounding:**\n   104\t    *   `AVSS`, `CVSS`, `DVSS`, `REFHM`, and `PAD` are tied to the local GND.\n              
                             105\t    *   **System Grounding:** A note specifies that \"GND is tied to CELL0 at connector via a thick             
                             trace,\" establishing the reference potential for the low-voltage side.\n   106\t\n                                  
                             107\t**Communication Interface Details:**\n   108\t*   **Isolated Path (via U2):**\n   109\t    *   **TX             
                             (MCU -> BMS):** `USB2ANY_TX_3.3` (J17-7) -> U2 (INB->OUTB) -> `RX_CO` -> J21 -> `RX` (U1-52).\n   110\t              
                             *   **RX (BMS -> MCU):** `TX` (U1-53) -> U2 (INC->OUTC) -> `USB2ANY_RX_3.3` (J17-8).\n   111\t    *                  
                             **Fault (BMS -> MCU):** `NFAULT` (U1-62) -> J2 -> `NF_J` -> U2 (IND->OUTD) -> `NFAULT_C` (J17-3).\n                  
                             112\t    *   **Power:** U2 Isolated side powered by `USB2ANY_3.3V`. BMS side powered by `CVDD` via                   
                             J18.\n   113\t*   **Direct Path (Non-Isolated):**\n   114\t    *   **J3 (Direct UART Header):**\n                    
                             115\t        *   Pin 1: GND.\n   116\t        *   Pin 2: `NFAULT` (Schematic) / \"FAULTn\" (Text).\n                 
                             117\t        *   Pin 3: `RX_C` (Schematic) / \"RX\" (Text).\n   118\t        *   Pin 4: `TX` (Schematic)             
                             / \"TX\" (Text).\n   119\t        *   **Conflict:** The text description for J3 pins 4 and 5 (\"4 RX\",              
                             \"5 TX\") contradicts the schematic wires (Pin 4 is `TX`, Pin 3 is `RX_C`). The schematic wires are                  
                             assumed correct: Pin 3 is Input (RX), Pin 4 is Output (TX).\n   120\t    *   `RX` (BMS) can be driven                
                             from `RX_C` (J3-3) via R119 (100\u03a9) and J1.\n   121\t    *   `TX` (BMS) connects directly to J3-4.\n             
                             122\t\n   123\t**Auxiliary Measurement Inputs (BBP/BBN):**\n   124\t*   **Pins:** `BBP` (Pin 64) and                 
                             `BBN` (Pin 63) on U1.\n   125\t*   **Path 1 (Bus Bar - DNP):**\n   126\t    *   Inputs: `BBP_CELL` and               
                             `BBN_CELL`.\n   127\t    *   Filtering: Differential RC filter formed by R9/R12 (402\u03a9) and C10                  
                             (0.47\u03bcF).\n   128\t    *   Connection: Connects to `BBP`/`BBN` via R10/R13 (0\u03a9). Currently                 
                             DNP.\n   129\t*   **Path 2 (Current Sense - Active):**\n   130\t    *   Inputs: `SRP_S` and `SRN_S`.\n               
                             131\t    *   Filtering: Optional C11 (0.47\u03bcF, DNP).\n   132\t    *   Connection: Directly wired to              
                             `BBP`/`BBN`. (Note: R17 is shown as DNP across the lines, likely a placeholder).\n   133\t    *                      
                             **Conflict Note:** The schematic shows both paths merging at the `BBP`/`BBN` nets. Since Path 1                      
                             resistors are DNP, Path 2 is the active source.\n   134\t\n   135\t**Cell Balance (CB) Configuration                 
                             Path:**\n   136\t*   **R25** connects `CB12` to `CB13`\n   137\t*   **R21** connects `CB13` to `CB14`\n              
                             138\t*   **R26** connects `CB14` to `CB15`\n   139\t*   **R22** connects `CB15` to `CB16`\n   140\t\n                
                             141\t**Voltage Sense (VC) Configuration Path:**\n   142\t*   **R27** connects `VC12` to `VC13`\n                     
                             143\t*   **R23** connects `VC13` to `VC14`\n   144\t*   **R28** connects `VC14` to `VC15`\n   145\t*                 
                             **R24** connects `VC15` to `VC16`\n   146\t\n   147\tIn the current DNP state, all these lines                       
                             (`CB12`-`CB16` and `VC12`-`VC16`) are electrically isolated from each other within this specific                     
                             block.\n   148\t\n   149\t**Temperature Measurement Subsystem:**\n   150\t*   **Reference Power:**                   
                             `TSREF` (Thermistor Reference) connects to the `PULLUP` rail via jumper **J5**.\n   151\t*   **Divider               
                             Network:** The `PULLUP` rail feeds 8 parallel voltage dividers. Each divider consists of a 10.0k top                 
                             resistor (e.g., R7) and a bottom NTC thermistor (e.g., RT1) to GND.\n   152\t*   **Measurement Points:**             
                             The midpoint of each divider is labeled `GPIOx_R` (e.g., `GPIO8_R`, `GPIO7_R`... `GPIO1_R`).\n   153\t*              
                             **GPIO Interface (J4):**\n   154\t    *   **J4** allows connecting the BMS IC's `GPIOx` pins (odd pins               
                             1-15) to the measurement points.\n   155\t    *   **Channels 2-8:** `GPIOx` connects directly to                     
                             `GPIOx_R` when the jumper is placed.\n   156\t    *   **Channel 1:** Unlike channels 2-8, Channel 1                  
                             includes an intermediate filter stage. The divider node `GPIO1_R` (with C60 and D3) connects via R128                
                             (1k) to `GPIO1_C`. `GPIO1_C` then connects to J4 Pin 2. Thus, the BMS pin `GPIO1` measures the filtered              
                             divider voltage through a 1k series resistor.\n   157\t    *   **TP44** provides a test point on the                 
                             `GPIO1_R` net (the divider node).\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t# Uncertainties, Assumptions &                        
                             Confidence\n   161\t\n   162\t*   **Assumption:** The numbers 12 through 16 in the configuration block               
                             represent the cell index in the stack.\n   163\t*   **Uncertainty:** The destination of the vertical                 
                             lines (`CBxx`/`VCxx`) is now confirmed to be U1 on one side, but the connection to the actual battery                
                             connector/filter components is not yet visible.\n   164\t*   **Uncertainty:** Why only GPIO1 has the                 
                             explicit filter/protection circuit (R128, C60, D3) shown.\n   165\t*   **Uncertainty:** The exact nature             
                             of D3 (24V). It appears to be a bidirectional TVS or Zener pair for overvoltage protection.\n   166\t*               
                             **Resolved:** The main IC is identified as TI BQ79616PAPQ1.\n   167\t*   **Resolved:** `CB` and `VC`                 
                             lines connect to the main IC.\n   168\t*   **Resolved:** `TSREF` source is U1 Pin 51.\n   169\t*                     
                             **Uncertainty:** The labels \"BBN_CELL\" and \"BBP_CELL\" in the Bus Bar section appear swapped relative             
                             to the port symbols. I have assumed the port symbols are correct.\n   170\t*   **Uncertainty:** The                  
                             exact nature of `SRP_S`/`SRN_S`. They are likely \"Sense Resistor Positive/Negative Sense\" lines, but               
                             it is unclear if they come from a raw shunt or an amplifier. Given the direct connection to the BMS IC's             
                             auxiliary ADC inputs, they are likely raw shunt voltages (or slightly filtered), assuming the BMS IC has             
                             a suitable input range (usually +/- 200mV or similar for current sense).\n   171\t*   **Uncertainty:**               
                             R17 is DNP and placed across the `SRP_S`/`SRN_S` lines. It might be a placeholder for a differential                 
                             filter resistor or a zero-ohm short for testing.\n   172\t*   **Uncertainty:** The purpose of U2 `INA`               
                             (Pin 3) being tied to GND via R123. It might be an unused channel or a configuration pin.\n   173\t*                 
                             **Uncertainty:** U2 `OUTA` (Pin 14) appears unconnected.\n   174\t*   **Resolved:** Q1 is active, Q2 is              
                             DNP. The NPN supply circuit is populated.\n   175\t*   **Conflict:** J3 pinout text vs schematic wires.              
                             Text says Pin 5 is TX, Pin 4 is RX. Schematic wires show Pin 4 is TX, Pin 3 is RX_C. Schematic wires are             
                             assumed correct.\n   176\t\n   177\t# Library Mapping\n   178\t\n   179\t| Designator | Component Name |             
                             Library Location |\n   180\t|------------|----------------|------------------|\n   181\t| U1 |                       
                             BQ79616PAPR | /app/lib/imports/BQ79616PAPR.tsx |\n   182\t| U2 | ISO7342FCQDWRQ1 |                                   
                             /app/lib/imports/ISO7342FCQDWRQ1.tsx |\n   183\t| Q1 | MMBT3904LT1G | /app/lib/imports/MMBT3904LT1G.tsx              
                             |\n   184\t| D1 | 150060GS75000 | /app/lib/imports/A_150060GS75000.tsx |\n   185\t| D3 | BZX84C24 |                  
