                                     "type": "text",                                                                                              
                                     "text": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on                                                            
                             /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/tscircuit_operation_manual.md:             
                             \n     1\t# `tscircuit` Operational Guide\n     2\t\n     3\t## Circuit Assembly, Modules &                          
                             Connectivity\n     4\t\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t## Overview\n     8\t\n     9\tThis guide                     
                             describes **how to assemble circuits using `tscircuit`** by:\n    10\t\n    11\t* instantiating existing             
                             components\n    12\t* organizing them into modules\n    13\t* arranging schematic and PCB layouts\n                  
                             14\t* defining connectivity using nets and traces\n    15\t\n    16\tIt assumes that **all components                
                             referenced already exist** and are importable.\n    17\t\n    18\t---\n    19\t\n    20\t## 1. Circuit               
                             Structure\n    21\t\n    22\t### Root Container\n    23\t\n    24\tEvery circuit must be wrapped in a                
                             `<board />` element.\n    25\t\n    26\t```tsx\n    27\t<board width=\"100mm\" height=\"80mm\">\n                    
                             28\t  {/* circuit contents */}\n    29\t</board>\n    30\t```\n    31\t\n    32\t* `<board />` is the                
                             root of schematic and PCB generation\n    33\t* All components, nets, groups, and traces must be                     
                             children of `<board />`\n    34\t\n    35\t---\n    36\t\n    37\t## 2. Using Existing Components\n                  
                             38\t\n    39\t### A. Built-in Primitives\n    40\t\n    41\t`tscircuit` provides globally available                  
                             primitives that **do not require imports**.\n    42\t\n    43\tCommon examples:\n    44\t\n    45\t*                 
                             `<resistor />`\n    46\t* `<capacitor />`\n    47\t* `<inductor />`\n    48\t* `<diode />`\n    49\t*                
                             `<led />`\n    50\t* `<jumper />`\n    51\t* `<pinheader />`\n    52\t\n    53\t#### Required Props for              
                             Passives\n    54\t\n    55\t| Element         | Required Props                     |\n    56\t|                      
                             --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n    57\t| `<resistor />`  | `name`,                          
                             `resistance`, `footprint`  |\n    58\t| `<capacitor />` | `name`, `capacitance`, `footprint` |\n                     
                             59\t| `<inductor />`  | `name`, `inductance`, `footprint`  |\n    60\t| `<led />`       | `name`,                    
                             `color`, `footprint`       |\n    61\t\n    62\tExample:\n    63\t\n    64\t```tsx\n    65\t<resistor\n              
                             66\t  name=\"R1\"\n    67\t  resistance=\"10k\"\n    68\t  footprint=\"0603\"\n    69\t/>\n    70\t```\n             
                             71\t\n    72\t---\n    73\t\n    74\t### B. Imported Components\n    75\t\n    76\tComponents defined                
                             elsewhere (e.g., ICs or reusable blocks) may be imported and instantiated.\n    77\t\n    78\t```tsx\n               
                             79\timport { ControllerIC } from \"./lib/ControllerIC\"\n    80\t\n    81\t<ControllerIC name=\"U1\"                 
                             />\n    82\t```\n    83\t\n    84\t* Imported components are treated as black boxes\n    85\t* Pin names             
                             must be used exactly as exposed by the component\n    86\t\n    87\t---\n    88\t\n    89\t## 3. Nets\n              
                             90\t\n    91\t### Declaring Nets\n    92\t\n    93\tNamed nets are used for shared electrical nodes.\n               
                             94\t\n    95\t```tsx\n    96\t<net name=\"VCC\" />\n    97\t<net name=\"GND\" />\n    98\t```\n                      
                             99\t\n   100\t* Nets should be declared near the top of the `<board />`\n   101\t* Nets may be                       
                             referenced anywhere within the board\n   102\t\n   103\t---\n   104\t\n   105\t### Connecting to Nets\n              
                             106\t\n   107\tPins may be connected directly to nets.\n   108\t\n   109\t```tsx\n   110\t<trace                     
                             from=\".U1 > .VDD\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n   111\t<trace from=\".U1 > .GND\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n                        
                             112\t```\n   113\t\n   114\t---\n   115\t\n   116\t## 4. Connectivity\n   117\t\n   118\t### A.                      
                             Point-to-Point Traces\n   119\t\n   120\tUse `<trace />` to connect two pins.\n   121\t\n                            
                             122\t```tsx\n   123\t<trace from=\".U1 > .TX\" to=\".R1 > .pin1\" />\n   124\t```\n   125\t\n   126\t*               
                             `from` and `to` use CSS-like selectors\n   127\t* Pin identifiers depend on the component definition\n               
                             128\t\n   129\t---\n   130\t\n   131\t### B. Mixed Connectivity\n   132\t\n   133\tBoth nets and direct              
                             traces may coexist.\n   134\t\n   135\t```tsx\n   136\t<trace from=\".C1 > .pin1\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n               
                             137\t<trace from=\".C1 > .pin2\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n   138\t```\n   139\t\n   140\t---\n   141\t\n                   
                             142\t## 5. Modular Organization with `<group />`\n   143\t\n   144\t### Purpose\n   145\t\n                          
                             146\t`<group />` is a container for organizing related components and traces.\n   147\t\n   148\tIt may              
                             be used to:\n   149\t\n   150\t* cluster functionally related elements\n   151\t* simplify layout\n                  
                             152\t* move multiple elements together\n   153\t\n   154\t---\n   155\t\n   156\t### Auto-Layout                     
                             Support\n   157\t\n   158\t`<group />` supports automatic layout for schematic and PCB.\n   159\t\n                  
                             160\t#### Schematic Layout Props\n   161\t\n   162\t* `schFlex`\n   163\t* `schFlexDirection=\"row\" |               
                             \"column\"`\n   164\t* `schGap`\n   165\t\n   166\t#### PCB Layout Props\n   167\t\n   168\t*                        
                             `pcbGrid`\n   169\t* `pcbGridCols`\n   170\t* `pcbGridGap`\n   171\t\n   172\t---\n   173\t\n   174\t###             
                             Example: Power Input Block\n   175\t\n   176\t```tsx\n   177\t<group\n   178\t  schFlex\n   179\t                    
                             schFlexDirection=\"row\"\n   180\t  schGap=\"2mm\"\n   181\t  pcbGrid\n   182\t  pcbGridCols={2}\n                   
                             183\t  pcbGridGap=\"1mm\"\n   184\t>\n   185\t  <resistor name=\"R_Fuse\" resistance=\"10\"                          
                             footprint=\"0603\" />\n   186\t  <capacitor name=\"C_Bulk\" capacitance=\"100uF\" footprint=\"1206\"                 
                             />\n   187\t\n   188\t  <trace from=\".R_Fuse > .pin2\" to=\".C_Bulk > .pos\" />\n   189\t</group>\n                 
                             190\t```\n   191\t\n   192\t---\n   193\t\n   194\t## 6. Placement\n   195\t\n   196\t### Manual                     
                             Placement\n   197\t\n   198\tComponents or groups may be positioned explicitly.\n   199\t\n   200\t*                 
                             Schematic: `schX`, `schY`\n   201\t* PCB: `pcbX`, `pcbY`\n   202\t\n   203\t```tsx\n   204\t<capacitor\n             
                             205\t  name=\"C1\"\n   206\t  capacitance=\"100nF\"\n   207\t  footprint=\"0402\"\n   208\t  schX={10}\n             
                             209\t  schY={5}\n   210\t  pcbX={12}\n   211\t  pcbY={8}\n   212\t/>\n   213\t```\n   214\t\n                        
                             215\t---\n   216\t\n   217\t### Placement Strategy\n   218\t\n   219\t* Manual coordinates are typically             
                             used at **top-level**\n   220\t* Auto-layout is preferred inside dense groups\n   221\t\n   222\t---\n               
                             223\t\n   224\t## 7. Canonical Assembly Example\n   225\t\n   226\t```tsx\n   227\timport { ControllerIC             
                             } from \"./lib/ControllerIC\"\n   228\t\n   229\texport default () => {\n   230\t  return (\n   231\t                
                             <board width=\"100mm\" height=\"80mm\">\n   232\t      <net name=\"VCC\" />\n   233\t      <net                      
                             name=\"GND\" />\n   234\t\n   235\t      <ControllerIC name=\"U1\" />\n   236\t\n   237\t                            
                             <capacitor\n   238\t        name=\"C_Decouple\"\n   239\t        capacitance=\"100nF\"\n   240\t                     
                             footprint=\"0402\"\n   241\t      />\n   242\t\n   243\t      <trace from=\".U1 > .VDD\" to=\"net.VCC\"              
                             />\n   244\t      <trace from=\".U1 > .GND\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n   245\t      <trace from=\".C_Decouple              
                             > .pin1\" to=\"net.VCC\" />\n   246\t      <trace from=\".C_Decouple > .pin2\" to=\"net.GND\" />\n                   
                             247\t    </board>\n   248\t  )\n   249\t}\n   250\t```\n   251\t\n   252\t---\n   253\t\n   254\t## 8.               
                             Built-in Elements Reference\n   255\t\n   256\t| Element                           | Description                     
                             |\n   257\t| --------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n   258\t| `<board />`                  
                             | Root container            |\n   259\t| `<net />`                         | Named electrical node                   
                             |\n   260\t| `<trace />`                       | Electrical connection     |\n   261\t| `<resistor />`               
                             | Passive resistor          |\n   262\t| `<capacitor />`                   | Passive capacitor                       
                             |\n   263\t| `<inductor />`                    | Passive inductor          |\n   264\t| `<diode />`                  
                             | Diode                     |\n   265\t| `<led />`                         | LED                                     
                             |\n   266\t| `<jumper />` / `<solderjumper />` | Configuration links       |\n   267\t| `<pinheader />`              
                             | Connector                 |\n   268\t| `<group />`                       | Layout container                        
                             |\n   269\t| `<subcircuit />`                  | Isolated functional block |\n   270\t| `<via />`                    
                             | PCB via                   |\n   271\t| `<testpoint />`                   | Measurement access                      
                             |\n   272\t| `<hole />`                        | Mechanical hole           |\n   273\t\n   274\t\n",                 
                                     "enable_truncation": true                                                                                    
                                   }                                                                                                              
                                 ],                                                                                                               
